# Clean Up Test Artifacts

After browser testing, screenshots, automated test runs, or diagnostic logging, delete temporary artifacts before finishing the task.

## Delete when done

- Screenshots and captures (`*.png`, `*.jpg`, `*.webp`) saved for verification — e.g. `asset-matrix*`, `screenshot*`, `browser*`, `verified*`
- Temporary dumps (`tmp_*.json`, `tmp_*.py`, curl/API capture files)
- Agent-browser output files (use explicit paths or temp paths printed by the CLI)
- Test-only log files created during the session

## Do not delete

- Source code, configs, lockfiles, or `.git`
- Intentional product assets (e.g. `**/public/**` images used by the app)
- Operational application logs unless they were created solely for the current test

## Workflow

1. Prefer writing test artifacts outside the repo or to clearly temporary names/paths.
2. When verification is complete, delete every artifact you created.
3. Before ending the task, scan the workspace root, `tmp/`, `.tmp/`, and agent output dirs for leftovers.
